 "_doc": "Hand transcriptions read by tools/lay_1871_street_furniture.py (T-3805): the fire-alarm telegraph's street boxes as Edwards' 1871 directory lists them, the year's new fire hydrants at a named corner as the Board of Public Works' Tenth Annual Report lists them, and the barbers and tobacconists the directory's classified pages put at a named corner. Text is the printed words with the OCR's errors corrected by eye; `streets` are the 1871 context's names for the printed ones (Fifth Avenue is South Wells Street's 1870 name), null where the station is a building, not a corner. djvu_line is the line in the Internet Archive item's djvu.txt (edwardsannualdir141871chic).",
